t is not, it answers Q1-Q4 with reasoned dispositions.  That last check exists because this project once scored a 26,992-byte ECHOED BRIEF as the best answer in its panel. *** ONE MISMATCH, AND IT IS MINE, AND IT IS A GENUINE APPARATUS FINDING RATHER THAN A SEAT FAILURE. *** The ruling quotes CHECKPOINT.md&#x27;s first line as `2026-09-16 ~22:2x ...&#x27;; the file now reads `2026-09-17 ~01:2x ...&#x27;.  **I REFRESHED THE CHECKPOINT HEADER WHILE FABLE WAS STILL RUNNING**, so the quote is verbatim-correct for the file AS IT WAS WHEN THE SEAT READ IT, and I invalidated the seat&#x27;s own liveness proof underneath it.  Everything else in the line -- the HEAD stamp 9c91999 and the full trailing text -- matches exactly, which is what shows the seat really read the file. &gt; **THE RULE THIS BUYS: THE FILE-QUOTE LIVENESS CHECK REQUIRES THE QUOTED FILE TO BE STABLE FOR THE DURATION OF THE SEAT&#x27;S RUN.**  The echo test proves prompt delivery AND file access by asking for a verbatim quote -- and it silently stops proving the second half if the quoted file is edited mid-flight.  A mismatch then reads as a DEAD OR HALLUCINATING SEAT when the seat was neither.  Quote a file nothing in the round is going to touch, or freeze the quoted line for the run. *Caught only because the verifying subagent was told IN ADVANCE to distinguish a timestamp-only difference from a real failure -- had it not been, a correct Fable ruling would have been recorded as failing its own liveness check.* — evidence: FABLE_RULING_20260917.md, 15,116 b; token FABLE_ADJ_20260917 at line 12; MODEL line at line 17</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ-ATTACKS-ITS-OWN</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** FIVE OF THE TWELVE ACCEPTED DISPOSITIONS DO NOT SURVIVE, AND THE SEAT SAYS THE WORST OF THEM IS ITS OWN. ***  It was asked to be HARDER on findings that had been accepted, precisely because a ruling in your favour is the one you are least likely to test, and it did exactly that. (1) ITS OWN O1 IS WRONG AS DERIVED -- the decline arm has no switch, relative_addr is read at exactly one place (the fatal() format string) and flows into no lvalue and no test.  **112 should not be written down anywhere.**  Converges with agy, glm and deepseek, reached independently. (2) **MY NINE-ENTRY ANSWER IS WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS AT ONCE.**  Nine ENTRIES is TWELVE obligations (entries 1, 3, 8 are blind in BOTH latch states and owe a carrier in each: 8 pre + 4 post = 12) -- which is an ENTRY count spent as a ROW count, THE EXACT SUBSTITUTION A1 WAS ACCEPTED FOR REFUTING four sections earlier.  FOUR OF THE NINE CAN CARRY NO ROW AT ALL: 1 and 3 because the prelude re-forces REV and the non-window arm body is empty; 4 and 8 because a 4-byte read takes the HIGH LANE and answers 0, which is what a declined read answers too; 40 because it is already filed HOST-DIAGNOSTIC.  AND IT IS ALSO TOO SMALL: buckets8.py line 88 unpacks `val` and never uses it, so ten +0x08 write entries collapse onto two keys while the CONTROL arm DOES branch on the value.  Value-aware the obligations are 27, not 12. (3) **THE #499 WIDTH-AXIS SHAPE IS SITTING INSIDE THE ROW ADDED TO CLOSE THIS FAMILY**: entry 14 (sd +0x08 = 0x0201) is uncovered with a direct oracle, because the row at probe:1256 counts the `sw&#x27; form and not its `sd&#x27; twin -- same address, same value, other width, no row.  The value-aware derivation predicted the split BEFORE the seat read that line. (4) A11&#x27;s remedy is MEASURABLY VACUOUS -- lw +0x08 returns 0 and a declined read returns 0, so the row is green under its own mutant.  The non-vacuous form already exists UNSHIPPED in ctl4r.py as a PAIR (ctl4r -&gt; 0 with ctl0c -&gt; 0x100), so A11 and A12 are one finding from two ends. (5) A13 was accepted AND NOT APPLIED TO ITS OWN SECTION: its `6 of 6&#x27; is precisely the metric A13 condemns.  Row-content record is 5 of 6, and the FORWARD record is 1 of 2. *** AND IT MEASURED THE ONE THING O4 ONLY DERIVED: M5_revlatch 188/188, A SECOND TOTAL ESCAPE, with M6_istlatch 185/188 as the negative control -- the identical edit at INTSTAT reds three rows, so the detector CAN see this shape and simply cannot see it at REV.  The decline x latch-SET face has TWO MEASURED open cells, so the mandate is EARNED on the decline side rather than inherited from my framing. *** **A RULE GAP, and it is the part that outlives the round:** every floor clause enumerates from what the guarded body READS, WRITES or TESTS -- and a goto over a dispatch does NONE of those, because its content is an OMISSION.  Proposed bounded clause: A SUPPRESSING GUARD&#x27;S FLOOR AXES ARE THE AXES OF WHAT IT SUPPRESSES, NOT OF WHAT IT DOES, restricted to labels of the skipped dispatch whose arms have a non-null body for that direction.  Sent to Fable as the round&#x27;s rule question. ITS OWN ERRORS, recorded by it rather than by me: it built TWO classifiers before trusting either and BOTH keyed on correlates -- one reproducing the row-to-session off-by-one its own pass-1 answer had already recorded.  Only the VALUE-axis finding survived, because it rests on `val&#x27; being unused at line 88, a fact about the source.  FOOTPRINT CLEAN: sentinel absent, cmp-clean, binary newer than source, restored byte-identical to base, all four fork copies still md5 8c1d1545. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/opus_adjudication.md (42 KB); opus_pass1_work/ logs M5_revlatch and M6_istlatch, both CRIMEP_DONE; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/codex.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ-REFUTES-O4-DISCRIMINATOR</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **IT REFUTED O4&#x27;s DISCRIMINATOR, WHICH I HAD CALLED `SURVIVING INTACT&#x27;, AND THE REFUTATION IS THE PROBE ITSELF.**  O4 derived the open decline cells from `does any session refuse at this label more than once?&#x27;.  codex: session 30 performs BOTH `lb TIME&#x27; and `lh TIME&#x27; AFTER another refusal has already set the latch, asserts their zero answers, and NEVER SAMPLES THE CLOCK EFFECT AFTERWARD.  CHECKED by reading probe lines 984-995: the `lh +0x30&#x27; at 984 is the first refusal, and the refused TIME reads sit at 992 and 993 with only value rows after them.  **So the discriminator is NOT SUFFICIENT, and the probe comment at 1077-1079 that the Opus seat cited as `the probe already knew&#x27; IS STALE -- a preceding repair added exactly those accesses.**  The conclusion (REV/TIME open) may still hold, but for a different reason: not `never refused twice&#x27; but `refused twice and never sampled for the effect&#x27;. **AND IT SHARPENED A7 IN A WAY THAT WOULD HAVE SAVED A VACUOUS ROW:** for an INTSTAT 4R VALUE assertion the seed&#x27;s UPPER 32 BITS must be nonzero.  CHECKED at dev_sgi_ip32.c:291-294 -- INTSTAT is +0x10, so relative_addr &amp; 4 == 0 and the read takes `odata &gt;&gt; 32&#x27;.  Seeding SOFTINT|HARDINT nonzero in the LOW half reads 0, and the new row would have been VACUOUS: the exact failure repair 14 exists to end. It also holds that an ENTRY count, an OBSERVABLE OBLIGATION count and an ASSERTION count are three different quantities, and that `more than the mirror means the criterion is wrong&#x27; -- a test I wrote into the packet -- is not a valid upper bound.  It UPHOLDS the one-diff mandate on the project rule independently, and requires the disposition table to name REACHABLE INPUT/STATE, OBSERVED EFFECT, DISCRIMINATING ASSERTION and any EQUIVALENCE ARGUMENT -- neither `nine carriers&#x27; nor `112 cells&#x27; repairs that evidentiary gap. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/opus_adjudication.md (42 KB); opus_pass1_work/ logs M5_revlatch and M6_istlatch, both CRIMEP_DONE; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/codex.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — NO-GO on repair 14 as proposed; GO-WITH-CHANGES for a restructured one closing the four accept-side pre-blind cells {21, 46, 32, 33} and the two decline-side latch-set cells (TIME, REV).  **IT REFUTED THE FINDING I HAD CALLED THE FINDING OF THE ROUND:** the decline arm is NOT a second 56-cell product -- dev_sgi_ip32.c:296-320 and :411-423 show it has NO SWITCH and never branches on relative_addr.  The arm&#x27;s own partition is {latch}, two cells. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/; regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/ADJUDICATION_findings.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** THE PASS DOES NOT CLOSE #529, AND IT REJECTED BOTH READINGS I OFFERED. ***  I asked whether &#x27;killed on their named rows&#x27; means AT LEAST ONE or ALL.  grok named a third thing: SPLIT KILL FROM CHANNEL.  &#x27;At least one&#x27; is the check-that-cannot-fail -- naming all 204 rows would then pass -- and it is the reading that lets me close, so it is refused.  check_pred.py ALREADY implements the third thing (exact set equality), so A PREDICTION MISS IS L4 OF PRETABLE, A WRONG RECORD, FIXED IN THE RECORD AND NOT BY ADDING ROWS.  Q1: G_lane_ctl&#x27;s sole-carrier at 203/204 is NOT a floor breach.  Q3: my grade (completeness defect, not floor) upheld -- but my REASONING was refuted: I wrote &#x27;whatever it scored would have matched&#x27; and check_pred.py puts M1_gotolatch in MUST_STAY_KILLED, so a 204/204 would have printed REGRESSION and CHECK_PRED12_FAIL.  The cannot-fail part is the SET, not the KILL.  *** THE UNASKED FINDING IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS: `acc ctl0c&#x27; NEVER REDS UNDER ANY OF THE FIFTEEN LEGS, including the equivalent-cell decline the PAIR exists to observe -- so the DISCRIMINATING half of the pair carries no measured kill.  A row is not discharged by existing.  Do NOT add a row; run a decline that reaches 0x0c, or stop claiming ctl0c as the channel. ***  And a FALSE CONTRACT CLAIM, verified in dev_sgi_ip32.c before recording: the default: arm is NOT host-log-only for acc ctl0c -- the width arm runs BEFORE the switch and 0x0c/8 == 0x08/8, so a 4-byte read takes CONTROL&#x27;s LOW half and a decline answers 0.  Guest-visible.  Latent hazard recorded though it did not fire: check_pred.py still slices ln[:15], the same padded-column family as #530&#x27;s bug. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/grok_pass2_20260917.txt; its brief BRIEF_pass2_20260917.md; the three L4 corrections it produced are in L4_CORRECTIONS_20260917.md; the contract correction landed in regress/crime_width_probe.py&#x27;s header</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ-CLI</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — TRANSPORT: the kimi CLI (FILE-READING).  **BOTTOM LINE: KEEP THE MANDATE; REPLACE THE MAP.**  Nine accept-side carriers (7 rowable + 2 disclosure), two decline-side rows (REV in-window, TIME with a DOWNSTREAM READ), and Part C must enumerate the 8 unlistable bucket members or carry the debt -- **and when it cites O4, CITE THE BLINDNESS, NOT THE REFUSAL COUNT**, which converges exactly with codex&#x27;s independent refutation of O4&#x27;s discriminator. *** IT CORRECTS A CLAIM OF MINE: I called mirror14.py an INDEPENDENT tool confirming buckets8.py&#x27;s N_PRE_BLIND=8.  It is not independent -- same capture machinery, same regexes, same latch-split rule, same probe source, with the row-attribution off-by-one fixed.  `A systematic capture bug would agree in both.&#x27;  The 8=8 agreement is CORROBORATION, not independence, and I overstated it. *** It also corrects O8&#x27;s warrant in detail: cpu-&gt;is_32bit is dead on ip32 via isa_level **4** (mips_cpu_types.h:75), not `R4400 -&gt; isa_level 3&#x27;.  Both give is_32bit == 0, so the conclusion holds and the reason was wrong -- **the FOURTH instance this round of a right conclusion reached by a route that does not carry it.** NOTED HONESTLY BY THE SEAT: it ran no gate, so it did not settle the mutant SCORES, and it names the check anyone attacking them should use -- **diff M3/M4&#x27;s red row SETS against the prediction file, not the counts** -- which is A13&#x27;s lesson applied forward. IT ALSO CONFIRMED MY OWN REMEDIATION: the OUTSTANDING_BUGS stale citation now cites :728 with the macepci correction clause, and it says so rather than re-filing it. *** ONE DISAGREEMENT LEFT OPEN FOR FABLE: kimi says 7 of the nine are ROWABLE; the Opus seat says FOUR of the nine can carry no row at all (leaving 5).  They cannot both be right and neither ran a mutant to settle it. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/kimi.txt and ollama_kimi.txt; PANEL_COMPLETE 01:17:59, 8/8</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **THE SHARPEST FORM OF THE REFUTATION: O1 CONTRADICTS A10, WHICH I ACCEPTED IN THE SAME DOCUMENT.**  A10 (codex) says the accept side is REACHABILITY-CONSTRAINED, not a cross-product; O1 then builds the decline side AS a cross-product by analogy -- the same error with opposite signs, ratified in one breath.  Derived, the decline arm is 7 labels x 2 latch = 14, of which 12 are covered or equivalent and 2 are exactly O4&#x27;s rows.  ALSO UPHELD, two more of my acceptances overstated: `O1 supersedes D1 entirely&#x27; is false because O8 itself demotes codex&#x27;s reachability to CONDITIONAL (it holds only because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8), so D1 is NARROWED AND STILL OPEN; and `O7 answers the 4b residual doubt&#x27; is false because O7 is a DIFFERENT blindness mechanism (unlistable bucket members) from the 4b one (a third session passing the 26-or-40 test while carrying no oracle).  I collapsed two holes into one. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/; regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/ADJUDICATION_findings.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — Same refutation, reached from INSIDE the packet: O1&#x27;s 56 is an ANALOGY contradicted by a DERIVED figure in the same answer -- O4 derives 7 decline x latch-set cells and its discriminator asks only whether a session refuses at a label more than once, mentioning neither len nor R/W.  *A packet-fed seat found a self-contradiction that I ratified twice.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_004011/; regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/ADJUDICATION_findings.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-ADJ</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **FOUND THAT MY A2 EVIDENCE WAS INSUFFICIENT, AND IT WAS RIGHT.**  For my reading to refute P4 (`CLEAR driven by session 40 ALONE&#x27;), the gate-run session must be a DIFFERENT session from 40 -- and I never established that.  My cited evidence (gate-run calls POST() nowhere and drives INTMASK 4R at :735 before its first refusal at :741) is entirely CONSISTENT with gate-run BEING session 40.  **CHECKED: the conclusion survives on evidence I had not cited** -- BUCKETS8_rerun.out entry 25 shows `lw +0x18 IMK&#x27; driven latch-CLEAR by [20, 40], TWO DISTINCT sessions, so ALONE is false on the buckets output rather than on my reading.  *** THIS IS THE THIRD TIME THIS ROUND A SEAT FOUND MY REASON WRONG WHILE MY CONCLUSION HELD (agy on the early-return, opus on `it is silent&#x27;, now minimax here).  The pattern is worth naming: right answers by routes that do not carry them, and a wrong reason gets reused. *** ALSO UPHELD as a PACKET defect: A13 asserted a 12 -&gt; 13 correction without showing its arithmetic.  The count rose because a THIRTEENTH LEG LANDED after I wrote 12, not because of the row-note issue -- but minimax could not know that, because the packet never said so. — eviden