yte` STILL USES THE SUBSTRING FORM.**  Verified at `regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1608`: `&quot;ran&quot; if &quot;Transfering&quot; in t else &quot;no&quot;`.  It is a DIFFERENT cell (the SUCCESS arm&#x27;s shadow-clear pair-oracle) and `accept dma` is the print site clause (b) was measured against, so this is not a (b) hole -- **but it is the old form left sitting beside the repair of it**, which is the shape a future reader mistakes for a decision. **(4) `nodata notx` counts `t.count(&quot;Transfering&quot;)`** -- harmless for a decline row wanting 0, and NOT a pin of the number. **(5) THE ROW STILL DOES NOT PROVE 408 BYTES MOVED.**  `accept data` (want `0x10` at the destination) remains the movement oracle; the tightened `accept dma` proves the LOG LINE carries the count.  The contract must not be read as claiming otherwise. DISPOSITION: FILED, not fixed.  The stopping rule takes in-round only a MEASURED FALSE PASS or a WRONG RECORD; the wrong record in this family was the `EXPECT_ROWS`/clause-(c) conflation and it was corrected in place the same day.  (1) and (2) are contract-honesty items -- they matter exactly if the probe header&#x27;s &quot;prints data_len&quot; bullet is read as &quot;UNIQUELY data_len&quot;, which it should not be.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class=