* the malloc. — evidence: regress/artifacts/allocsize_20260917/HUNT_grok_20260917.txt</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">probeblockingwait</span><span class="ttl">maple_dmaaddr_probe.py uses a BLOCKING waitpid, so on the mapledmahang path it would hang the harness forever instead of reporting -- the mirror of the false-green class, and outside probedeathoracle&#x27;s WNOHANG-keyed census</span><span class="tip">maple_dmaaddr_probe.py uses a BLOCKING waitpid, so on the mapledmahang path it would hang the harness forever instead of reporting -- the mirror of the false-green class, and outside probedeathoracle&#x27;s WNOHANG-keyed census — note: *** `regress/maple_dmaaddr_probe.py` CALLS `os.waitpid(pid, 0)` -- A BLOCKING WAIT -- AFTER `rd(10.0)`, AND `mapledmahang` IS A PATH ON WHICH THE EMULATOR NEVER EXITS. ***  If that probe ever drives a maple DMA list with no LAST bit, the blocking wait **never returns and the harness hangs**, reporting nothing at all.  **This is the mirror of the false-green class closed today as `probedeathoracle`.**  That one was about a probe reporting ALIVE for a dead process; this is a probe that cannot report anything because it waits forever on a process that will not die.  Both come from keying an oracle on process death without a deadline -- and `probedeathoracle`&#x27;s census keyed on `WNOHANG`, so a BLOCKING `waitpid` was outside its population by construction. **The remedy is the same shape as the one already applied: a DEADLINE.**  A blocking `waitpid` in a harness that can drive a non-terminating guest path needs SIGKILL-after-N rather than patience.  Filed rather than fixed: it is a real hazard on a path nothing currently drives, and the fix belongs with whichever round builds the `mapledmahang` witness, because that round is the one that will first make the path reachable.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</spa