ks like an answer. **AND MY OWN AUDIT OF IT UNDER-COUNTED 9 AS 6**, because the pattern I checked required a severity token `(LOW|MED|HIGH)` and three headings carry only `(closed)`.  *Sixth correlate-keyed check of this session, committed inside the audit of the fifth.* Codex&#x27;s real verdict, recorded now: **CLOSE 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8; KEEP-OPEN 3, 5, 9.**  *** L4 -- MY &#x27;SPLIT BY SEAT CLASS&#x27; ADJUDICATION IS A WRONG RECORD, AND THE FABLE SEAT SHOWED IT IS FALSE ON THE PACKET&#x27;S OWN DATA.  Corrected 2026-09-17. ***  I wrote that the four FILE-READING seats reached CLOSE 1-8 / KEEP-OPEN 9 while the PACKET-FED seats kept rows open. **Codex is file-reading and its verdict line reads `CLOSE 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8.  KEEP-OPEN 3, 5, 9`** -- I tabulated it as CLOSE 1-8.  Meanwhile minimax (packet-fed) CLOSED rows 1 and 5, kimi-sub CLOSED 1/3/4/6/7, glm CLOSED 1/3/4/6/7/8.  **The classes do not sort the verdicts.** *** AND THE RULING WAS CIRCULAR, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING. ***  My own brief&#x27;s S0 told the seats *&quot;an unsettleable row stays open, which is the safe direction&quot;* -- which converts every honest not-checkable into a KEEP-OPEN vote -- and I then read those votes back as evidence that the doctrine was working.  **I instructed the behaviour and then cited it as a finding.** **THE RULING FORM THAT SHOULD HAVE BEEN WRITTEN** sorts the packet-fed KEEP-OPENs BY KIND, not by class: (a) NOT-CHECKABLE-FROM-PACKET, *discharged by naming the file* -- row 2&#x27;s condition (c), row 8&#x27;s figures, deepseek&#x27;s rows 1/3/4/6/7 -- where *&quot;the file-reading seats verified it&quot; is the right answer ONLY when the file is named*; and (b) SUBSTANTIVE, adjudicated on merit regardless of class -- row 9 (all four right), row 5&#x27;s arithmetic, row 5&#x27;s unnamed labels (raised by kimi-sub and glm, the SAME finding as codex and opus5, so a class split puts those seats on the wrong side of their own finding). *** AND ONE SUBSTANTIVE PACKET-FED CLAIM WAS FALSE AND A CLASS RULING IS EXACTLY HOW IT GOES UNREFUTED: *** glm&#x27;s *&quot;nothing pins the suppression side, 0x08 must NOT fire&quot;* is answered by the row `a routine 0x08 preserves the command` in `diff_wdc_identify.c`.  **That deserved a refutation by file, and my ruling gave it a category instead.** **THE COST OF THE MIS-STATEMENT:** it hid codex&#x27;s row-3 dissent (the row now re-opened on a measurement), and it converted a three-seat finding on row 5 into &quot;the file-reading seats said CLOSE&quot;.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **KEEP-OPEN** (already `in work`).  `HEAD` is `&quot;Transfering&quot; in t`; the working tree is `&quot;Transfering 408 byte