he probe&#x27;s internal `t&#x27;.  A preserved probe log answers what the ROWS scored, never what the GUEST printed. ***  REPAIR IS ORACLE-ONLY: row count unchanged at 62, every row NAME identical (diffed against the pre-edit copy), so the gate pin stays 62 and the named-row list needs no edit.  DISCLOSED, NOT CLAIMED: the literal pins 408 because that is what THIS session&#x27;s staging produces; a future round changing the staged size must RE-DERIVE it rather than assume it. — evidence: regress/artifacts/gdromdmadefault/acceptdma_20260917/VERDICT.md and logs/; sentinels KILLACCEPTDMA_DONE 16:50:19 and LEG3_DONE 17:07:48</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">untrackeddetectors</span><span class="ttl">regress/crime_width_probe.py and regress/lca_isalane_probe.py are UNTRACKED -- two shipped, measured detectors exist in no commit, and the checker that said so was reporting it as &#x27;no such file&#x27;</span><span class="tip">regress/crime_width_probe.py and regress/lca_isalane_probe.py are UNTRACKED -- two shipped, measured detectors exist in no commit, and the checker that said so was reporting it as &#x27;no such file&#x27; — note: crime_width_probe.py is the instrument behind today&#x27;s #529 ctl0c discharge (202/204); lca_isalane_probe.py is the 352-row #530 detector and the file the lcaisaphys witness spec copies its helpers from.  A fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments.  check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s domain() is `git ls-files&#x27; (COMMITTED-OR-STAGED, per its own docstring) while its GHOST message said &#x27;regress/ has no such file&#x27; -- a wrong record that discredited a true finding; corrected the same day.  150 GHOST rows: 148 per-round artifact copies, exactly 2 top-level detectors.  *** CORRECTED SAME HOUR: the exposure is PROSPECTIVE, not present.  The COMMITTED gate_arm.sh has ZERO references to crime_width_probe (git show HEAD:regress/gate_arm.sh | grep -c) -- only the MODIFIED working copy invokes it at :1658.  A fresh clone today is consistent.  THE REAL FINDING IS A COMMIT-ORDERING CONSTRAINT: gate_arm.sh and crime_width_probe.py MUST be staged in the SAME commit, or the commit itself creates a battery invoking a missing file.  lca_isalane_probe.py is in no gate and carries no such constraint.  Neither probe has an EXPECT_ROWS identity row (floor clause (c)); both have a _DONE sentinel and a _RESULT= line.  I wrote &#x27;a fresh clone has the measurements and not the instruments&#x27; from the working tree without asking git what HEAD contains.  *** RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-18, AND THE EXPOSURE IS WIDER THAN THE ROW SAID. ***  `git ls-files --error-unmatch&#x27; confirms BOTH detectors are untracked: regress/crime_width_probe.py (119,216 bytes) and regress/lca_isalane_probe.py (99,545 bytes) -- 214 KB of SHIPPED, MEASURED detector code that exists in no commit.  AND THE BROADER FIGURE: `git status --porcelain regress/&#x27; reports **149 untracked paths** under regress/, which now includes EVERY #531 artifact -- all three killtable dirs, all three PRETABLE blocks, the opus seat&#x27;s preserved logs, and the frozen 18-row instrument.  A working-tree loss today destroys the two detectors AND the entire evidence base for #531&#x27;s floor discharge.  *** NOT RESOLVED THIS CYCLE, AND THE REASON IS CONTENTION, NOT OVERSIGHT: *** the fix is a COMMIT (staging protects nothing), a commit owes its targeted gate, and a gate is CPU-heavy while an opus5 measuring seat is in flight.  Queued for the moment that seat lands.  Constraints carried: stage BY NAME, never `git ad