t against working-tree loss -- only a commit does&#x27;.  A row whose headline says RESOLVED IN SUBSTANCE and whose tail says STILL OWED is read by its headline.  *** AND THE SCOPE IS TWO FILES, NOT 147: *** `git status --porcelain regress/&#x27; reports 147 untracked paths today, of which 145 are ARTIFACTS directories belonging to rounds in flight (56 crimewidthkill, 16 lcaisaphys, 8 alphavmkill, 8 wdcaltdigin, 6 ppcrlwhighhalf, 3 alphaifetchkill, ...).  EXACTLY TWO are probes.  NEITHER IS MINE TO STAGE: crime_width_probe.py belongs to #529, which my standing constraints forbid me to touch, and arm_msrmode_probe.py belongs to `armmsrmodekill&#x27;, an open HIGH nobody has started.  They land with their own rounds&#x27; commits.  The row&#x27;s TITLE is also half stale -- it names lca_isalane_probe.py, which is now tracked; the live pair is crime_width_probe.py and arm_msrmode_probe.py.  OWNER QUESTION OPEN from both sessions: commit them, exclude them from the hygiene census, or leave the census counting them.  *** AND THE OBJECT DB SETTLES THE CAUSE, 2026-09-21 -- raised by the peer session, RE-MEASURED HERE, and it produced a fact neither of us had. ***  Staging writes a blob that a reset does not remove, so `git fsck --unreachable&#x27; is the witness: **18 unreachable blobs whose first line names crime_width_probe.py** (the peer counted 13 on a narrower pattern), with loose-object mtimes clustering at 2026-09-19 03:43:07 and one at 09-14 -- so that file WAS staged, repeatedly.  The peer&#x27;s `git reset -q&#x27; ran ~06:1x the same morning, just before 7836071, and they record the loss as theirs with the honest caveat that a later reset by anyone would look identical.  **arm_msrmode_probe.py has ZERO matching blobs: never staged by either session**, which matches `git log&#x27; returning nothing for it.  *** THE SHARPER FACT, AND IT STRENGTHENS THE ROW: the file&#x27;s CURRENT content is not in the object DB EITHER. *** `git hash-object regress/crime_width_pro