SWER and its 8.7 KB answer was nearly discarded — note: *** A LIVE SEAT WAS REPORTED MISSING, AND THIS FILE&#x27;S OWN COMMENT PREDICTED IT IN THOSE WORDS. ***  `adjudicate.sh&#x27; fires its cloud seats in one loop and CHECKS them in a second, and the second must carry the ${m%%:*} SHORT FORM of the first because that is how the output filenames are built.  The 2026-08-29 migration glm-5.3-flash -&gt; glm-5.3 changed the FIRE loop and not the CHECK loop.  So the run wrote glm-5.3.txt while the check hunted glm-5.3-flash.txt, and it printed `glm-5.3-flash: NO ANSWER (0b)&#x27; and `ADJUDICATORS: 2/3&#x27;.  *** glm HAD ANSWERED WITH 8,693 BYTES, FOUR DEFECTS AND THE SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT FINDING IN THE ADJUDICATION -- an oracle that would have certified a live defect GREEN. ***  The comment immediately above the broken line reads: &#x27;Updating the fire loop alone would leave this one looking for glm-5.2.txt, which the run never writes -- so a LIVE seat would be reported as a missing one.  That is the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape arriving through a rename rather than through a wall.&#x27;  The structure knew; the edit did not.  FIXED 2026-09-17: both loops now agree on glm-5.3.  Note the fix is a RETYPE and therefore has the same failure mode next migration -- deriving the check list from the fire list with ${m%%:*} is the structural form and is NOT done here, because it changes a script every adjudication runs and owes its own negative controls.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — The seat-check loop kept the superseded `glm-5.3-flash` tag after the fire loop migrated to `glm-5.3` on 2026-08-29, so the run wrote `glm-5.3.txt` while the check hunted `glm-5.3-flash.txt`.  A