td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">changelogroundgap</span><span class="ttl">seven rounds shipped code with no CHANGELOG round block -- four unmentioned anywhere in the file, and two of them are the rounds the vacuity floor was minted from</span><span class="tip">seven rounds shipped code with no CHANGELOG round block -- four unmentioned anywhere in the file, and two of them are the rounds the vacuity floor was minted from — note: *** SEVEN ROUNDS SHIPPED CODE WITH NO CHANGELOG ROUND BLOCK, AND FOUR OF THEM ARE UNMENTIONED ANYWHERE IN THE FILE.  Measured 2026-09-17 against a live denominator of 293 round-block headings. ***  The ethos line is *&#x27;a CHANGELOG.md round block per correction&#x27;*, and `#436 #439 #441 #443 #466 #487 #493` each have **zero** headings matching their number.  Twelve commits across the seven, every one verified present in `refs/heads/main`. *** NONE IS A VOID NUMBER, WHICH IS THE CHECK THAT MAKES THIS A DEFECT RATHER THAN A GAP IN A COUNTER. ***  This project HAS a void number (`#289`), so a skipped heading is not automatically a breach -- it is one only if the number shipped.  All seven did, and three are ordinary defect fixes: **`#441 sh4bcr`** (*two guest instructions ended the emulator process*), **`#443 sh4pcicexit`** (*one guest LOAD ended the host, on 116 of 137 offsets*), and **`#493 wdcaltoffset`** (*a rung-3 witness for a live sev-high defect*). *** AND THE SHARP PART: `sh4bcr` AND `sh4pcicexit` ARE THE TWO ROUNDS THE VACUITY FLOOR WAS MINTED FROM. ***  The carrier cites them by name as its founding evidence -- *&quot;sh4bcr&#x27;s first detector passed a mutant reinstating the very host kill its round removed; sh4pcicexit&#x27;s passed the original kill verbatim&quot;* -- so **the most-cited exemplars in the whole rule set have no round block in the file a reader would go to.**  A future reader re-deriving the floor&#x27;s warrant finds the rule, finds the rounds named, and finds nothing in the CHANGELOG under either number. **THE GAP IS DIRECTIONAL AND IT IS THE INVERSE OF THE USUAL ONE.**  This session&#x27;s other records findings are all *written down but wrong*; this one is *shipped but not written down*, which no gate looks for -- section H checks seats were fired, G checks an answer was recorded, and `check_cited_artifacts.py` checks a cited path exists.  **Nothing asks whether a round that shipped has a block at all.** **DISPOSITION: recorded, NOT reconstructed.**  Writing seven retroactive round blocks from commit messages would manufacture records, which is worse than the gap -- so ONE consolidated *assessed-not-changed* entry names every round and its commits, and the reconstruction is filed for a round that can do it from the rounds&#x27; own artifacts. *The checker that would close this is a ledger-row-to-CHANGELOG-heading existence test, forward-only from a cutoff -- the `check_bugfile_sync.py` idiom.  FILED, not built: it is a tooling change owing two negative controls, and this file&#x27;s own rule is that such a change ships as its own harness round rather than as a rider.*  DERIVER, because a count in a durable record names the command that made it and the tree it ran against (HEAD at the time of writing, working tree clean of CHANGELOG edits):
 
     for n in 436 439 441 443 466 487 493; do
         printf &#x27;#%-4s heading=%s any=%s\n&#x27; &quot;$n&quot; \
@@ -15908,7 +15739,7 @@ WITNESS: none built, and the honest note is that a rung-3 witness may be IMPOSSI
 
 *** AND THE FIRST FORM OF THAT DERIVER WAS KEYED ON A CORRELATE, WHICH I CHECKED BEFORE TRUSTING IT. ***  `^#+ .*#NNN\b` tests the LITERAL number, while the class is *is this round documented* -- and a RANGE heading (`## #89-#94`, which this file really does use) reports 0 for a round it documents.  Checked: no range heading covers any of the seven, and the bracketing headings confirm each gap (R9=#435, R10=#437 straddle #436; R12=#440, R13=#442 straddle #441).  *The correlate would have produced a plausible wrong answer in the direction that manufactures a finding.* — evidence: regress/artifacts/recordsaudit_20260917/RECORDS_grok_20260917.txt; CHANGELOG.md; git log --all --format=&#x27;%h|%s&#x27;</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open">